# The build context is the repository root (infra/docker-compose.yml). Dockerfile.api copies only
# named paths under apps/api, so nothing below reaches the image; this keeps secrets, the database
# files and caches out of the context sent to the builder.
.git/
# Settings files at any depth: a nested one (apps/client, say) would reach the web build, and Expo
# bundles its EXPO_PUBLIC_ values into the page. No image needs the example file, so it goes too.
#
# No `!` exceptions anywhere in this file. A wildcard exception makes the builder walk every
# excluded folder to look for matches, and on Linux infra/volumes/postgres belongs to the database's
# user (mode 0700), so a build after the first `make up` fails with "permission denied" (CI run
# 42200877912). A plain-path exception would be safe, but keep the rule simple: none.
**/.env
**/.env.*
infra/volumes/
**/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.hypothesis/
**/.dev-mail/
**/node_modules/
*.log
.DS_Store
# The client's own build and test outputs: the web image builds its export afresh.
apps/client/dist/
apps/client/coverage/
apps/client/playwright-report/
apps/client/test-results/
apps/client/.jest-cache/
